---
description: Independent SDK and connector release rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Independent Releases

- Connector manifest metadata.version is the release source of truth. An
  unchanged version explicitly defers release.
- Declared versions equal the latest tag or advance by one patch, minor, or
  major step. First releases use v0.1.0.
- SDK tags use sdkgo/vX.Y.Z; connector tags use their module directory.
- Connector modules depend on an exact published SDK version without replace,
  pseudo-version, branch, or commit SHA.
- Release SDK changes before a later connector dependency-upgrade PR.
- When discovering an SDK contract gap, develop SDK and connector changes
  together with `go.work` or a temporary local `replace` and run the full
  connector verification. Never commit that `replace`. Before handoff, split
  the SDK changes into a preceding SDK PR, merge and release its tag, then pin
  that exact published SDK version from the connector PR.
- Run module verification with GOWORK=off. Connector releases run automatically
  after merge to main; manual runs only repair incomplete releases and catalog
  deployment.
- v0 breaking releases cannot be patch releases. v1+ breaking releases require
  a major module-path migration.
- Use one released module per PR unless a repository-wide mechanical change
  requires several.
- Use sdkgo:, connector(<slug>):, tooling:, or docs: subjects.
- Put exact lowercase (breaking) in the PR and final commit message for public
  breaking changes.
